{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-009", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "France defines terms for long-term capacity auction", "content": "<p>France's energy regulator has proposed the parameters for the country's first long-term capacity auction, covering the winter of 2030-31. The auction will target 82 GW of capacity, including 3 GW eligible for multi-year contracts, as France seeks to safeguard electricity supplies while limiting costs for consumers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/france-defines-terms-for-long-term-capacity-auction/\">France defines terms for long-term capacity auction</a> appear", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/france-defines-terms-for-long-term-capacity-auction/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-010", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Eskom kicks off tender for 6 GW of renewables-plus-storage", "content": "<p>South African utility Eskom has launched a qualification process to select strategic partners for up to 6 GW of renewable energy and storage projects. The portfolio will include at least 2 GW of solar and 1 GW/4 GWh of battery storage, with selected developers joining a five-year co-development and investment framework.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/eskom-kicks-off-tender-for-6-gw-of-renewables-plus-storage/\">Eskom kicks off tender for 6 GW of renewables-plus", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/eskom-kicks-off-tender-for-6-gw-of-renewables-plus-storage/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-011", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Multiple grounding points cut lightning-induced overvoltage in solar panels by up to 55%", "content": "<p>Researchers in Indonesia found that higher soil resistivity significantly increases lightning-induced overvoltage in PV systems. Their simulations also showed that multiple grounding points and connections closer to the lightning strike location can substantially reduce transient voltages.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/multiple-grounding-points-cut-lightning-induced-overvoltage-in-solar-panels-by-up-to-55/\">Multiple grounding points cut lightning-induced over", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/multiple-grounding-points-cut-lightning-induced-overvoltage-in-solar-panels-by-up-to-55/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-012", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Energy Dome opens CO2 battery manufacturing plant in Italy", "content": "<p>Energy Dome’s new manufacturing plant will supply components for long-duration energy storage (LDES) projects in India, the United States and Ireland. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/energy-dome-opens-co2-battery-manufacturing-plant-in-italy/\">Energy Dome opens CO2 battery manufacturing plant in Italy</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/energy-dome-opens-co2-battery-manufacturing-plant-in-italy/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-013", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Study identifies new PID degradation mechanism in medium-voltage PV modules", "content": "<p>French researchers have found that increasing PV system voltage significantly worsens potential-induced degradation (PID), with encapsulant conductivity playing a key role in module performance. They also identified a new degradation mechanism involving partial discharges and electrical treeing, highlighting additional reliability risks for medium-voltage PV modules.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/study-identifies-new-pid-degradation-mechanism-in-medium-voltag", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/study-identifies-new-pid-degradation-mechanism-in-medium-voltage-pv-modules/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-014", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South Korea details auction market to replace renewable quota system", "content": "<p>Draft rules for South Korea’s new renewables auction market provide for monthly difference payments from Korea Electric Power Corp. (Kepco), a separate track for projects up to 500 kW, and an exit route for renewable energy certificate (REC) spot-market sellers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/south-korea-details-auction-market-to-replace-renewable-quota-system/\">South Korea details auction market to replace renewable quota system</a> appeared first on <a href=", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/south-korea-details-auction-market-to-replace-renewable-quota-system/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "risen-2026-10-12-015", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["risen"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Risen releases 23.5%-efficient anti-glare heterojunction solar module", "content": "<p>Risen Energy has unveiled a new anti-glare heterojunction solar module featuring a dual-layer optical design and a power output of up to 730 W. The bifacial panel achieves a maximum efficiency of 23.5% and has received Class AAA anti-glare certification from TÜV Rheinland.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/risen-releases-23-5-efficient-anti-glare-heterojunction-solar-module/\">Risen releases 23.5%-efficient anti-glare heterojunction solar module</a> appeared first", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/12/risen-releases-23-5-efficient-anti-glare-heterojunction-solar-module/", "type": "rss"}]}
